{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790437422,"nonce":"2EtvJLcGmPtfNMw/AHQDdWQLgeU=","title":"Use a stable OpenCode session ID per tutor conversation","message":"The native Zen adapter sends x-opencode-session: gic-tutor for every conversation. OpenCode guidance for Go says this header should be one stable ID per conversation. Trace the native session identity through the typed Tauri boundary, keep it stable across turns and change it on a new conversation, and test header behavior without exposing credentials. This is a protocol correctness task, not a claimed fix for Big Pickle: bounded Zen requests with the fixed header and a distinct per-conversation header both returned HTTP 403, as did a request without tools. Diagnose the provider-side rejection separately.","files":null}]}